# Helix OTA — Environment configuration example
#
# Copy this file to `.env` (git-ignored) and fill in your values.
# NEVER commit the actual `.env` file (per §11.4.10).
#
# Full documentation: docs/guides/environment.md (if it exists) or
# refer to the script that reads each variable.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Release and recording prefix (§11.4.151, §11.4.155)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# HELIX_RELEASE_PREFIX sets the project-name prefix used for:
#   - Release tags:   <PREFIX>-<version>              (§11.4.151)
#   - Recording files: <PREFIX>---<scope>---<run-id>   (§11.4.155)
#
# When unset/empty, the prefix falls back to the lowercased
# snake_case project-root directory name (e.g. "helix_ota").
#
# Set ONLY when the default directory-based prefix is wrong for
# your checkout (e.g. a CI clone under a generic temp dir name).
#HELIX_RELEASE_PREFIX=helix_ota

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Container / artifact distribution targets (operator mandate 2026-06-22)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Remote container distribution runs via SSH + remote ROOTLESS `podman
# compose` (§11.4.161) on the distribution host. The mechanism lives in the
# helix layer at scripts/distribute_stack.sh (rsync a self-contained deploy
# bundle → `podman compose up -d` ON the remote → remote health-check) — it
# is NOT inside the generic containers submodule (§11.4.28). It is an
# EXPLICIT, on-demand action:
#
#   bash scripts/distribute_stack.sh --dry-run   # probe + print plan only
#   bash scripts/distribute_stack.sh             # real deploy (first ready host)
#
# Targets, in order of preference (first reachable WITH rootless podman wins):
#
#   1. thinker.local — LIVE. Passwordless SSH key (user milosvasic) works,
#                      rootless podman 4.9.3 + podman-compose 1.0.6 + the
#                      `podman compose` plugin (§11.4.161), Linux.
#   2. amber.local   — SSH key WORKS, but rootless podman is NOT yet installed
#                      there (`podman --version` → not found). distribute_stack.sh
#                      SKIPS amber honestly until the operator installs rootless
#                      podman on it (no bluff per §11.4.6); it is NOT a
#                      podman-ready distribution target yet.
#
# nezha.local is NO LONGER a container-distribution target (operator
# decision 2026-06-22). Reading / importing FROM nezha is still allowed,
# and nezha remains the Android EMULATOR host
# (scripts/boot_android_emulator.sh, SSH_HOST) — that is NOT distribution.
#
# The per-commit path (scripts/commit_all.sh, scripts/git_hooks/pre-commit)
# stays LIGHTWEIGHT — it only needs a reachable HelixTrack endpoint for the
# workable-items sync and does NOT fire a remote deploy on every commit.
# Set HELIX_DISTRIBUTE_ON_COMMIT=1 to opt routine commits into invoking
# scripts/distribute_stack.sh (default OFF).
#
# Expectation for every distribution host: passwordless SSH key auth for
# the configured user + rootless podman available (§11.4.161 — no sudo,
# no rootful). Overrides (space-separated candidate list + user):
#HELIXTRACK_REMOTE_HOST="thinker.local amber.local"
#HELIXTRACK_REMOTE_USER=milosvasic
#HELIX_DISTRIBUTE_ON_COMMIT=0
#HELIX_DIST_REMOTE_DIR=~/helix-dist

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Credential / secret configuration
# Add per-service .env.* files as needed (git-ignored).
# Example: .env.database, .env.registry
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
